    <string name="calibrate_help_title">Calibrate</string>
    <string name="calibrate_help_body">Point the camera at the sender\'s light with the light OFF, then tap Calibrate. MorseLight spends a couple of seconds measuring the average brightness in the box and locks it as a baseline. After that a flash reads as light whenever it rises above the baseline, and dark when it falls back. Re-run Calibrate whenever you move or the lighting changes.</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_title">Sensitivity</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_body">MorseLight first measures the average brightness in view (the \"avg\" reading). Sensitivity is how far above that average a flash must rise to count as light — a higher percentage demands a brighter, more obvious flash.\n\nRaise it if the room is bright or the reading flickers to \"Reading\" on its own. Lower it if the sender\'s light is dim or far away and short flashes are being missed.</string>
    <string name="detection_area_help_title">Detection area</string>
    <string name="detection_area_help_body">The blue box in the middle of the viewfinder is the region whose brightness is measured — everything outside it is ignored.\n\nShrink it to focus tightly on a small or distant light and shut out surrounding glare. Widen it for a nearby or slightly moving source so it stays inside the box.</string>
